From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 03:08:05 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 116/161] hjviewer: the home says who is logged in, a session
 window's login points at the main window (UX-H1)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

U26: the desktop home has an account line under the password's card, the phone's under the
remote ID field: "로그인됨 · name" (the display name only, never the portal ID) or
"로그인하지 않음" with a plain [로그인] when the window has no other (not while P1 or G2 has the
filled one or G3 shows). A press opens Settings -> Account (a phone's settings tab). In an
account build the desktop settings start with the account tab and open on it.

U33: a login in a Windows session window shows a toast that the main window has the note about
this PC (the main window does not come to the front). On an installed Windows PC the login
dialog says under its fields that a login there adds the PC to My PCs.

D16 (1.8.2 screen review carry-over): the logged-in devices list puts its arrow and
[로그아웃시키기] at the title's line on rows of two or three lines too.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
